# Citation metadata of skforecast-ai (https://citation-file-format.github.io).
# GitHub builds its "Cite this repository" button from this file, and Zenodo
# takes the metadata of each release (description, keywords, authors) from it.
# There is no `version` or `date-released` on purpose, as in skforecast: Zenodo
# takes both from each GitHub release, and the version to cite is the one
# listed on Zenodo. The authors are in the order of the published citations.

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: skforecast-ai
message: >-
  If you use skforecast-ai in a scientific publication, please cite the
  version you used. The DOI below always resolves to the latest release, and
  the DOI of each version is listed on Zenodo.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Javier
    family-names: Escobar Ortiz
    email: javier.escobar.ortiz@gmail.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0005-4399-7634'
  - given-names: Joaquin
    family-names: Amat Rodrigo
    email: j.amatrodrigo@gmail.com
    orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0009-0001-9531-9828'
repository-code: 'https://github.com/skforecast/skforecast-ai'
url: 'https://ai.skforecast.org/'
abstract: >-
  skforecast-ai is an AI forecasting assistant for time series built on
  skforecast. A deterministic, rule-based engine profiles the data, chooses
  the forecaster, estimator, lags, metric and cross-validation, and returns
  the forecast together with the skforecast script that produced it. An
  optional LLM layer explains the decisions and results, refines the plan on
  request and never changes a result on its own.
keywords:
  - time series
  - forecasting
  - time series forecasting
  - machine learning
  - skforecast
  - large language models
  - AI assistant
  - python
license: Apache-2.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21338159
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.21338159
    description: Concept DOI of skforecast-ai, resolves to the latest release.
